## 7. AI Generation Rules

### Generate

[What an AI agent can produce from this spec:]
- [e.g., All defined variants with correct token-mapped styles]
- [e.g., State transition CSS/JS for all states in section 3]
- [e.g., Accessible HTML with required ARIA attributes]
- [e.g., Storybook stories for each variant × state combination]

### Validate

[What the agent must verify before approving output:]
- [ ] All token references map to the parent L1 spec (spec_id: [SYSTEM-L1-NNN])
- [ ] All variants defined in section 3 are represented
- [ ] All states defined in section 3 are implemented
- [ ] Disabled state is keyboard-inaccessible AND aria-disabled is present
- [ ] Focus ring is visible in all variants
- [ ] Touch target minimum (44×44px) is met
- [ ] No raw color, spacing, or font values appear in output

### Forbidden

[What the agent must never generate:]
- Variants not defined in section 3
- States not defined in section 3
- Raw values for any property in the Token Usage table
- Implementations that violate any Do/Don't rule in section 6
- [Component-specific forbidden items]

### Prompt Seed

```
Generate a [Component Name] component for [System Name].

Reference: SDDn Behavior Spec [COMP-L2-NNN] v[version], inheriting from Foundation Spec [SYSTEM-L1-NNN] v[L1 version].

Requirements:
- Variants: [list from section 3]
- States per variant: default, hover, focus, active, disabled, loading, error
- All styles must use named tokens from [SYSTEM-L1-NNN] — no raw values
- Keyboard: Tab to focus, Enter/Space to activate
- ARIA: [specific requirements for this component]
- Touch target: minimum 44×44px

Do not generate: variants or states not in spec [COMP-L2-NNN], raw hex or spacing values.
```

